{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-26T10:24:23.440Z","author":"pm-github","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.2-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"6bdeb13ef1510979e5474a87","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.2-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"## What happens\n\nWhen a tracker item exists under the ID the importer reserves for an issue (`<prefix>-github-<hash>-<N>`) but was not created by the importer, the gated import refuses to run for the whole repository:\n\n> GitHub import target pm-vcs-github-c1741e698b48-228 is reserved for unbraind/pm-vcs#228, but its current owner is curated/unowned for content mirroring; importer creation provenance missing. Restore the intended GitHub provenance only if this item belongs to that issue; otherwise use a different configured ID prefix or tracker. …\n\nThis happened in three repositories on 2026-11-26 (pm-vcs issue 228, pm-rl issue 202, pm-ado issue 137): while the sync was down, agents that fixed those issues created the tracker item by hand under the reserved ID and tagged it `gh:owner/repo#N`.\n\n## What works (verified)\n\nSetting the declared field on the item links it explicitly, and the import then matches it by provenance:\n\n```\npm update <item> --field github_url=https://github.com/<owner>/<repo>/issues/<N>\npm github import <owner>/<repo> --state all --atomic --gate --dry-run   # plan verified, 1 matched by provenance\n```\n\n`--adopt-cited` alone does not help, and `pm github identity --identity … --owner …` needs a `--detach`, which does not fit a single item.\n\n## Expected\n\n1. The refusal names the repair: \"set `github_url` on this item to link it, or …\".\n2. The documentation for people and agents who start work on an issue says how to get its item: `pm github import <owner>/<repo> --issue <N>` (creates it with provenance), never a hand-created item under the reserved ID form.\n3. Optional: `pm create` refuses or warns when the requested ID matches the importer's reserved form and no `github_url` is set.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- The refusal text contains the repair command for the named item.\n- Tests: a hand-created item under the reserved ID with `github_url` set is matched; without it the refusal names the repair."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-github-github-ee4d59c27b67-286"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"A hand-created item under the importer's reserved ID stops the whole sync, and the refusal does not name the repair"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"GH issue #286: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/issues/286 · author @unbraind · created 2026-11-26T09:58:54Z · updated 2026-11-26T10:20:32Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["gh:unbraind/pm-github#286","github_author:unbraind"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-26T10:24:23.440Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-26T10:24:23.440Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"pm-github"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"7aa551bcddbf0314da1d7fe3849c17e37bffa9dd6cfb74817fb9b3e29fb5a8e6","item_hash_version":3,"message":"Imported from GitHub #286","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"f599c385e1014e735766c4212ef7f1369b16facfde4be0c090fd5bb6dca8605c"}
