{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-26T12:45:45.119Z","author":"pi-glm","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"2674fa95e556dd8d429b227d","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"update","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-26T12:45:45.119Z"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/status","value":"in_progress"}],"before_hash":"0ce117d3c2626fa4d6279d2b0aeb45834e6d8e3f965cc3e2b4d04353979caf97","after_hash":"d24193beaffe3ae65e52750e51522d394e22dd3c7bba79461d4299d7396f0b2d","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"353fa9c488e29e93af3b19dbe2b31a825b74beb473942cbe12de452e62ece8cc"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-26T12:45:53.885Z","author":"pi-glm","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"2674fa95e556dd8d429b227d","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/8","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-26T12:45:53.885Z","author":"pi-glm","text":"Re-review round 1 blocked the PR with three findings; continuing on the same branch, PR and item. Plan per finding, closing the class not the line:\n\n1. Repair command without the failing invocation's tracker selector (import-repair): general rule - a rendered repair command must replay the caller's tracker scope, like the host's revision-recovery scopeArgs. Fix: the reserved-ID repair command includes the tracker selector the failed import used, so copying it from any directory updates only that tracker. Search: every rendered repair/example command in the package that writes to a tracker item gets the same scope treatment.\n\n2. Repair offered on incomplete provenance (import-repair): general rule - a repair is offered only when applying it leaves exactly one consistent GitHub owner, evaluated with the same ownership-claims machinery the next import uses. Fix: the refusal carries the refused item snapshot and the offer is withheld unless the post-link claims are exactly the target issue. Search: every other adoption/link suggestion for the same precondition.\n\n3. Comment mirror stores source timestamps unvalidated (comment-mirror): general rule - external source timestamps are validated before persistence, like the importer's source-lifetime gate; a malformed value must count as a failed write and stay retryable, never be stored and skipped by marker. Search: every other path that persists source-provided timestamps.\n\nNon-blocking CodeRabbit out-of-scope check: factually wrong - the comment-mirror requirements are stated in issue #286's first comment (the non-convergent linked-item mirror), which this PR fixes alongside the reserved-ID refusal by design; the suggested alternative (link an issue that states the comment requirements) is already satisfied by that comment. Will strengthen the PR body's explicit link to it."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-26T12:45:53.885Z"}],"before_hash":"d24193beaffe3ae65e52750e51522d394e22dd3c7bba79461d4299d7396f0b2d","after_hash":"feab4ec99395a8be6b1bd0330e1c42beb81cdc806aff7d9b425b2ea40a1c5130","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"4eafdd75c4542b9f24411f21cedb3742262625dc1fd024186d61afb8935fdd00"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-26T13:14:32.835Z","author":"pi-glm","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"2674fa95e556dd8d429b227d","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/9","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-26T13:14:32.834Z","author":"pi-glm","text":"Round-1 blocking findings implemented on the same branch; no second PR, no new item.\n\n1. Scope replay: a new invocation scope (AsyncLocalStorage, same pattern the host uses for its own recovery scope) captures the typed tracker selector at the four command registrations that can render invocation-bound commands (github/gh-issues import, refresh, webhooks reconcile). The reserved-ID repair now renders pm --pm-path <the failing invocation's own spelling> update <id> --field github_url=<url>, matching the host's revision-recovery convention: replay the typed selector verbatim, keep an implicit (cwd/PM_PATH) selection implicit so a same-shell copy resolves the same tracker. Class search found two more invocation-bound rendered commands and fixed both the same way: the comment-mirror ownership-conflict release example (comment-mirror.ts) and the webhook reconcile recovery hint (webhooks.ts).\n\n2. Safe-link predicate: the curated/unowned refusal now carries the refused item snapshot non-enumerably (never serialized into diagnostics), and the link offer is kept only when the item's post-link ownership claims are exactly the target issue, evaluated with the same githubOwnershipClaims the next import uses. A reserved item with a contradicting github_number or github_repo keeps the plain refusal, so the offered repair can never create contradictory ownership that blocks the next import.\n\n3. Timestamp validation: the mirror validates each source comment timestamp before any write; a missing or unparseable one is counted failed and retried on the next sync, never stored and never skipped by its marker id. Item-level source lifetimes already had this rule (validateImportLifetime); the comment mirror was the one unvalidated persistence path in the package."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-26T13:14:32.835Z"}],"before_hash":"feab4ec99395a8be6b1bd0330e1c42beb81cdc806aff7d9b425b2ea40a1c5130","after_hash":"399fc6d76623f97dba51aebd6bbfebd44f54d598b489cc5b58eb107eaa26d2d4","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"faf027a5d21a098e1b7f58fa546cdf64df2e332755ca4149154f3eae2a94a443"}
